meta {
  name: Sessions - Send Message with Attachments
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/agents/:agent/sessions/:session/messages
  body: multipartForm
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
  agent: {{agentId}}
  session: {{agentSessionId}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  message: What does this file show?
  attachments[]: @file()
}

docs {
  The same request as "Sessions - Send Message", sent as multipart so files
  can ride along with the message. The streaming endpoint
  (`.../messages/stream`) accepts the same `attachments[]` field.

  - `attachments[]` — optional; up to
    `config('artifacts.message_attachments.max_files')` files (10 by
    default), each within `config('artifacts.max_upload_kilobytes')`.
    Allowed: images (JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP), PDF, and plain-text formats
    (txt, Markdown, CSV, JSON, HTML, XML, YAML). The type is detected from
    the file's own bytes; anything else is a `422`.

  Each file is stored as an artifact linked to the new user message and
  sent to the model with it — and again with that message on every later
  turn of the conversation. Attachments are never indexed into the agent's
  searchable knowledge.

  "Sessions - Messages" and "Sessions - Get" return each message's
  `attachments`.

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { message } }`.
}
